The Kepler-36 system: A pair of planets near 4:2 resonance that inquire the possible limits of planetary tidality
We present the discovery and analysis of Kepler-36, a planetary system with two planets, Kepler-36b and Kepler-36c, that have nearly identical densities and very different sizes.
